          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We have to check the sewing condition. First notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K := Cat(-,C)_\sim
              we have a natural bijection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
