                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi glue
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi glue
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K(D_1) \times_{K(D_{glue})} K(D_2)
                    \\simeq
                    K(D_1 \sqcup_{D_{glue}} D_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then recall from the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              that every functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
