            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
              \: In order for that to make sense, you need there to be a smallest sub-hyperstructure such that (blah). But I don’t see any reason for that to exist; the intersection of sub-hyperstructures need not be a hyperstructure. Even in a simplicial set the intersection of sub-Kan-complexes need not be a Kan complex; if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
