                    %mi X
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\cap Y
              may contain no filler at all.
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
              \: I agree that it is not a priori clear that some smallest hyperstructure with a given property exists. But I am not sure that I see what this has to do with intersections. Shouldn’t we we be looking at
              = succeed "?" do
                %em inclusions
            %p But in the particular case at hand, it feels that this smallest hyperstructure should certainly exist, no? I should think about formalizing it, but heuristically it should be given by the colimit over inclusions of the following steps for building it:
            %ul
              %li start with the interval cospans and take all ways to glue the interval with copies of itself.
            %ol
              %li
                %p then include for everey multi-cospan obtained so far also its product with the interval cospans;
              %li
                %p then form all composites of multi-cospans obtained so far
              %li
                %p then continue with 1. .
            %p
              %em> Mike
              \: In general, there are two ways to construct the smallest sub-widget of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that (blah):
            %ul
              %li
                Take the intersection of all sub-widgets of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                such that (blah).
              %li Start with (blah) and close it up, iteratively, under all the operations that define a sub-widget.
            %p Usually, if one works the the other does too. Occasionally one fails where the other succeeds due to set-theoretic technicalities. But here I think the problem is intrinsic and will rear its head wearing a different mask in either case.
            %p
              It definitely does not feel to me as though the smallest hyperstructure should exist. The problem with your proposal is when you say “form all composites.” Since composites are not an
              = succeed "," do
                %em operation
